Unpeel: smaller standard pages and no page preheat for the Host-side VT.

Why: the private "pty-core" design record, 'Round 3, Lane 3'. Upstream's standard page is
512 KiB and PageList.minMaxSize forces at least two pages, so any
max_scrollback under 1 MiB is silently raised to 1 MiB; page_preheat = 4
touches 8 x 16 KiB per terminal before a cell is written. Applied only when
building the vendored libghostty-vt.a for unpeel-host (build.sh); the app's
GhosttyKit build is untouched.

diff --git a/src/terminal/PageList.zig b/src/terminal/PageList.zig
index 7562286e8..d52688e74 100644
--- a/src/terminal/PageList.zig
+++ b/src/terminal/PageList.zig
@@ -31,7 +31,11 @@ const log = std.log.scoped(.page_list);
 /// too small will cause the pool to have to allocate more memory later.
 /// This should be set to some reasonable minimum that we expect a terminal
 /// window to scroll into quickly.
-const page_preheat = 4;
+///
+/// Unpeel: no preheat. Each preheated slot costs one resident OS page (the
+/// pool's free-list node) per screen before any output arrives; the Host
+/// runs hundreds of terminals and allocates pages on demand instead.
+const page_preheat = 0;
 
 /// The list of pages in the screen. These are expected to be in order
 /// where the first page is the topmost page (scrollback) and the last is
diff --git a/src/terminal/page.zig b/src/terminal/page.zig
index 0942e260c..6edba6827 100644
--- a/src/terminal/page.zig
+++ b/src/terminal/page.zig
@@ -1780,11 +1780,18 @@ pub const Page = struct {
 /// The standard capacity is chosen as the fast-path for allocation since
 /// pages of standard capacity use a pooled allocator instead of single-use
 /// mmaps.
+///
+/// Unpeel: a much smaller standard page than upstream's 512 KiB one, so
+/// PageList.minMaxSize (two pages) stays inside the Host's 256 KiB
+/// scrollback budget and a filled 80x24 terminal stays under 400 KiB
+/// resident. Styles and grapheme bytes are sized for a terminal that is
+/// read by a Host, not rendered; pages that need more grow to non-standard
+/// capacity exactly as upstream does.
 pub const std_capacity: Capacity = .{
     .cols = 215,
-    .rows = 215,
+    .rows = 32,
     .styles = 128,
-    .grapheme_bytes = if (builtin.is_test) 512 else 8192,
+    .grapheme_bytes = if (builtin.is_test) 512 else 2048,
 };
 
 /// The size of this page.
